/* The two rules above are theme.css copies, and this partial loads AFTER
   navigation-refresh.css — at an identical (0,2,0) they silently outranked the
   wide-menu anchors that file owns. A .nav-market-dd/.nav-mega-dd left
   `position:relative` makes the pill the offset parent, so the mega's `right:0`
   pinned a 1276px panel to the RIGHT EDGE OF ITS TRIGGER and hung the other
   ~950px off the left of the viewport (that is the split-panel artifact on
   special_situations.html and the other 58 vector-family pages). Restoring
   static also restores navigation-refresh's `content:none`: on a static parent
   the ::after bridge stops being a 9px strip under the pill and becomes one
   spanning the whole header, which keeps panels alive on any downward exit.
