/* ── Tier mark ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   The FIRST tier badge in the navigation (2026-08-07, Mastermind Bot). There
   was no lock/tier convention here before, so this rule IS the convention.

   STATIC AND UNCONDITIONAL — rendered identically for Free, Essential and Pro.
   That is the house tier-preview pattern (docs/TIER_PREVIEW_PATTERN.md): show
   every visitor the shell so a Free account can see what Pro buys, and let the
   server gate the payload. No JS, no /api/me call, no conditional markup —
   "hiding rows with CSS or a JS tier check is a marketing wall, not a gate".

   HUE-STABLE ON PURPOSE. It reads the menu's one interactive hue (--mock-blue),
   never the per-card icon accent, so a future PRO on a violet or cyan card is
   the same mark rather than a colour that means "cyan". Quiet by construction:
   9.5px against a 15px/650 title, hairline border, wash background, no hover
   state of its own — it labels, the title leads. Tier names are NAMED here and
   explained on plans.html; "PRO" is the tier's proper name in both languages
   (plans.html.j2 writes "Pro 试用" in Chinese), so it is deliberately untranslated
   and carries no t() twins. --mock-blue-deep is fallback-guarded for the brief
