rules.old:
/* Stock Dashboard governed presentation — canonical HK/Canada static shell.
   Canada extraction: theme-parity-tp1-canada-20260828-sol-001.
   Static-shell migration: prophet-cockpit-p0b-zero-fouc-20260904-sol-001.
   research/THEME_PARITY_RATCHET_PRESENTATION_CONVERGENCE_ARCHITECTURE.md §4-5.

   This paired plain-copy asset is loaded directly by both stock templates,
   before deferred enhancement. The generated HTML therefore owns a visible,
   styled product even when JavaScript or optional Canada evidence fails.

   Scope: everything lives under .mx-stockdash and its market modifiers.
   The composers keep their existing child class names and semantic adapters;
   outer-shell and owner-surface placement belong to server-rendered HTML.

   Token notes:
   - --r-ctl / --r-btn / --r-card / --r-panel / --r-pill are the DS-PR-0
     radius scale, not yet landed at :root (confirmed in templates/theme.css
     around its .skel/.mx-ladder comments). Every border-radius below uses
     the same var(--r-<family>, <canonical-px>) fallback idiom theme.css
     itself already uses for .skel/.aib-card/.mx-ladder — the fallback is
     the SCALE's own canonical stop (research/MASTER_PRODUCT_DESIGN_SYSTEM_V1.md
     §2.2: r-ctl 8, r-btn 10, r-card 12, r-panel 14, r-pill 999), never the
     pre-scale hand-authored pixel. Dark geometry therefore repaints by at
     most a couple of px per surface — a sanctioned migration-time snap, not
     a new decision — while the semantic token name is bound for when the
     scale lands at :root. See DARK DELTA item 5 below for the full mapping.
   - Elevation: var(--card-shadow) for flat panel/control surfaces.
     var(--popover-shadow)/var(--card-shadow) are the LIGHT overrides for the
     modal card and the segmented selected button; DARK keeps its own
     pre-extraction hand-authored geometry for those two surfaces instead,
     because the shared tokens alone under-elevate them on the dark plane —
     see DARK DELTA items 2-3 below.
   - Scrims/glows that were previously raw colour-function literals are
     recomposed with color-mix(in srgb, var(--bg|--text) N%, transparent),
     the same idiom templates/theme.css's own .af-scrim uses — see DARK
     DELTA item 4 below for what changed.
   - Action lane/stance identity reads the Prophet stance token family
     (var(--ink-pv-<tone>, var(--pv-<tone>))) for buy/wait/avoid, applied to
     both the stance chips and the Act-Now lane headers — never a
     market-direction literal. "Near" is the one exception: theme.css
     derives --pv-near FROM --pv-buy (a mix toward --muted), so painting a
     Near lane in --ink-pv-near reads as a paler Buy rather than a fourth
     independent hue — see DARK DELTA item 1 below. The Canada quote
     .nb-chg.up/.down convention (var(--ok)/var(--act), Western
     green-up/red-down even under ZH) is untouched.

   DARK DELTA — every rule below this list is the pre-extraction dark
   rendering, unchanged. These seven items are the only intentional dark
   changes this wave makes, each a restoration, a sanctioned migration
   snap, or a declared token-family alignment, never an undisclosed one:
     1. Near-lane header and Near stance chip repainted from the stance
        family (var(--ink-pv-near, var(--pv-near))) to the same
        informational ink every other "look, don't act yet" affordance on
        this estate already uses (var(--ink-link, var(--link)) — links, the
        "View all" control). The Task-3 extraction had instead bound Near to
        the stance family, which — because --pv-near derives from --pv-buy —
        collapsed Buy-vs-Near into two visually near-identical shades
        (measured pre-repair: their CIELAB separation fell from a wide
        double-digit gap to single digits on both planes). Restoring the
        link ink is what the pre-extraction runtime-injected CSS actually
        shipped; this is a repair, not a new hue choice.
     2. Modal card shadow: restored to a deep, widely-blurred, growth-offset
        geometry with its base colour token-derived from --bg (sub-perceptual
        difference from the prior hand-authored near-black literal). The
        extraction had substituted var(--popover-shadow) here, a shadow
        roughly a fifth the size — the dialog read nearly flat.
     3. Segmented-control selected-button shadow: restored to a tight, low,
        --bg-derived geometry (sub-perceptual vs. the prior literal) rather
        than var(--card-shadow), which likewise under-elevates it on dark.
     4. Modal/lane scrim base colour: token-derived from --bg rather than a
        hand-authored near-black literal — sub-perceptual, no visible change.
     5. border-radius snaps to the DS-PR-0 scale's canonical fallback (Token
        notes above): stance chip moves from 6 to 8, the segmented track
        moves from 9 to 10 (and its family moves from --r-ctl to --r-btn,
        preserving track>button nesting), the segmented buttons move from 7
        to 8, the Act-Now lane card moves from 11 to 12, the section panel
        moves from 13 to 14, the modal card moves from 15 to 14, the modal
        close control moves from 9 to 8, and the LIVE dot's own fallback
        moves from an ad hoc 50% to the scale's 999px pill stop (same
        rendered circle on a square box). Each move is at most a couple of
        px and is the sanctioned migration-time repaint the scale's rollout
        always implied.
     6. Buy lane header / Buy stance chip ink moved from the direction
        family (var(--ink-up, var(--up))) to the Prophet stance family
        (var(--ink-pv-buy, var(--pv-buy))) — a measured dark shift
        (CIELAB dE76 about 10 on the lane rail). Intentional: an action
        stance is not a market move, so it must not ride the direction
        tokens that flip under zh; the Prophet cards on this same page
        already print BUY in the stance family, and the lanes now agree
        with them.
     7. Avoid lane header / Avoid stance chip ink moved likewise from
        var(--ink-down, var(--down)) to var(--ink-pv-avoid,
        var(--pv-avoid)) — measured dark dE76 about 8. Same rationale as
        item 6; all four lane hues remain mutually distinct (minimum
        pairwise dE76 above 60 on both planes).
   The modal is now a descendant of the one static canonical main. */

.mx-stockdash {
  box-sizing: border-box;
  color: var(--text);
  font-family: var(--font-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, Inter, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif);
}
.mx-stockdash *,
.mx-stockdash *::before,
.mx-stockdash *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }

/* ---- Canada shell / head / Board+LIVE chips ------------------------------ */

.mx-stockdash--ca {
  width: min(1480px, calc(100% - 32px));
  margin: 22px auto 44px;
  font-size: 16.2px;
  line-height: 1.48;
}
.mx-stockdash--ca button,
.mx-stockdash--ca input,
.mx-stockdash--ca select { font-family: var(--font-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, Inter, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif); }

.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-head { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; min-height: 66px; margin-bottom: 14px; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-head h1 { margin: 0; font-size: 31.5px; line-height: 1.05; font-weight: 650; letter-spacing: -.03em; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-head-spacer { flex: 1; }

.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-chip,
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-live {
  height: 37px; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 7px; padding: 0 13px;
  border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--r-pill, 999px);
  background: var(--panel); color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600; white-space: nowrap;
}
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-quote-dot {
  width: 7px; height: 7px; border-radius: var(--r-pill, 999px);
  background: var(--muted); box-shadow: none;
}
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-quote-status b { color: var(--muted); }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-quote-status[data-quote-state="live"] .ca-v36-quote-dot {
  background: var(--ok); box-shadow: 0 0 9px color-mix(in srgb, var(--ok) 55%, transparent);
}
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-quote-status[data-quote-state="live"] b { color: var(--ok); }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-quote-status:is([data-quote-state="delayed"], [data-quote-state="stale"]) .ca-v36-quote-dot {
  background: var(--warn);
}
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-quote-status:is([data-quote-state="delayed"], [data-quote-state="stale"]) b {
  color: var(--ink-warn, var(--warn));
}

/* Fresh-signals cue (owner .pv-mk-new markers) in the Prophet header. */
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-fresh { color: var(--muted); font-size: 12.2px; white-space: nowrap; }

.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-lead-basis {
  height: 26px; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; padding: 0 9px;
  border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--r-pill, 999px);
  background: var(--panel2); color: var(--muted); font-size: 11px; font-weight: 650; white-space: nowrap;
}

/* ---- Section shells ------------------------------------------------------ */

.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-panel {
  margin-bottom: 14px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--r-panel, 14px);
  background: var(--panel); box-shadow: var(--card-shadow); overflow: hidden;
}
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-sec-hd { min-height: 54px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; padding: 0 15px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-sec-hd h2 { margin: 0; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 650; letter-spacing: -.012em; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-sec-spacer { flex: 1; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-link { color: var(--ink-link, var(--link)); font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-link:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-owner-panel > .panel,
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-card-grid > #standouts,
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-evidence-body > .panel {
  margin: 0; border: 0; border-radius: 0; background: transparent; box-shadow: none;
}
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-static-state { min-height: 72px; display: grid; place-items: center; }

/* ---- What to Act On Now: segmented control / lanes / rows / counts / routes / empty / View-all --- */

.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-body { padding: 4px 12px 5px; }

.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-seg { display: none; gap: 6px; margin-bottom: 10px; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-seg :is(button, a) {
  flex: 1; min-width: 0; height: 34px; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
  gap: 5px; padding: 0 7px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--r-ctl, 8px);
  background: var(--panel2); color: var(--muted); font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; cursor: pointer; text-decoration: none;
}
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-seg-t { min-width: 0; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-seg b { flex: none; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; font-weight: 700; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-body.is-enhanced .ca-v36-an-seg :is(button, a)[aria-selected=true],
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-body:not(.is-enhanced):not(:has(.ca-v36-an-lane:target)) .ca-v36-an-seg [data-ca-an-default=true],
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-body:not(.is-enhanced):has(#anv2-buy:target) .ca-v36-an-seg [href="#anv2-buy"],
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-body:not(.is-enhanced):has(#anv2-pull:target) .ca-v36-an-seg [href="#anv2-pull"],
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-body:not(.is-enhanced):has(#anv2-bot:target) .ca-v36-an-seg [href="#anv2-bot"],
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-body:not(.is-enhanced):has(#anv2-red:target) .ca-v36-an-seg [href="#anv2-red"] {
  color: var(--text); border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--text) 30%, var(--line)); background: var(--panel);
}
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-seg :is(button, a):focus-visible {
  outline: 2px solid var(--ink-link, var(--link)); outline-offset: 2px;
}

.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-lanes { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 10px; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-lane { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--r-card, 12px); background: var(--panel2); overflow: hidden; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-body .anv2-lane-body { padding: 0; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-disclosure { min-width: 0; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-disclosure:not([open]) > :not(summary) { display: none; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-body .anv2-lst .anv2-row {
  min-width: 0; padding: 0; overflow: visible; border-bottom: 0;
}
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-body .anv2-row-top {
  flex: 1; min-width: 0; align-items: stretch; gap: 0; margin: 0;
}
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-body :is(.anv2-chips, .anv2-stat) { display: none; }

.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-hd {
  display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 6px; padding: 8px 10px;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); border-top: 2px solid currentColor;
  font-size: 11px; font-weight: 750; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .02em;
}
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-hd.buy { color: var(--ink-pv-buy, var(--pv-buy)); }
/* Near is informational ("look, don't act yet"), not a fourth stance hue —
   theme.css derives --pv-near FROM --pv-buy, so painting Near in the stance
   family reads as a paler Buy. Bound to the same link ink every other
   "look, don't act yet" affordance on this estate uses. See the DARK DELTA
   note above (item 1). */
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-hd.near { color: var(--ink-link, var(--link)); }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-hd.wait { color: var(--ink-pv-wait, var(--pv-wait)); }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-hd.avoid { color: var(--ink-pv-avoid, var(--pv-avoid)); }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-hd b { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 700; }

.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-row-w { display: flex; align-items: stretch; border-top: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--line) 70%, transparent); }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-hd + .ca-v36-an-row-w { border-top: 0; }

.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-row {
  flex: 1; display: flex; min-width: 0; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 8px;
  min-height: 32px; padding: 5px 10px; border: 0; background: transparent; color: inherit;
  font-size: 12.6px; font-weight: 650; text-align: left; cursor: pointer;
}
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-row:hover:not(:disabled),
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-row.is-active { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--link) 6%, transparent); }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-row:disabled { cursor: default; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-name { min-width: 0; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-n { flex: none; color: var(--muted); font-size: 10.6px; font-weight: 600; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; white-space: nowrap; }

.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-go {
  flex: none; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; padding: 0 9px;
  border-left: 1px dashed color-mix(in srgb, var(--line) 80%, transparent);
  color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; text-decoration: none;
}
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-go:hover { color: var(--text); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--link) 6%, transparent); }

.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-empty { padding: 12px 10px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; text-align: center; }

.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-more {
  display: block; box-sizing: border-box; width: 100%; padding: 7px 10px; border: 0;
  border-top: 1px dashed color-mix(in srgb, var(--line) 80%, transparent);
  background: transparent; color: var(--muted); font-size: 11px; font-weight: 650; line-height: normal; cursor: pointer; list-style: none;
}
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-more::marker { content: ""; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-more::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-more:hover { color: var(--text); }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-more:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--ink-link, var(--link)); outline-offset: -2px; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-more .lm-hide { display: none; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-disclosure[open] > .ca-v36-an-more .lm-show { display: none; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-an-disclosure[open] > .ca-v36-an-more .lm-hide { display: inline; }

.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-empty-go {
  display: inline-block; margin-top: 10px; color: var(--ink-link, var(--link));
  font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none;
}
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-empty-go:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

/* ---- Leadership & Rotation: rows / rank / name / leaders / stance / count / basis --- */

.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-lead-cols { display: block; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-lead-col-h {
  display: flex; justify-content: space-between; padding: 11px 14px 10px;
  color: var(--muted); font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase;
}

.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-lead-row {
  position: relative; width: 100%; min-height: 58px; display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 30px minmax(0, 1fr) auto 34px; align-items: center; gap: 9px; padding: 10px 14px;
  border: 0; border-top: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--line) 72%, transparent);
  background: transparent; color: inherit; text-align: left; cursor: pointer; overflow: hidden;
  transition: .15s ease;
}
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-lead-row:after {
  content: ""; position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 0; width: var(--breadth, 8%); height: 1px;
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--link) 44%, transparent); opacity: .5;
}
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-lead-row:hover:not(:disabled),
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-lead-row.is-active { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--link) 6%, transparent); }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-lead-row:disabled { cursor: default; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-rank { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; color: var(--muted); font-size: 11.5px; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-lead-name { display: block; font-size: 14.7px; font-weight: 650; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-leaders { display: block; margin-top: 3px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 11px; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-count { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; color: var(--muted); font-size: 11.7px; text-align: right; }

.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-stance {
  height: 24px; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; padding: 0 9px;
  border: 1px solid currentColor; border-radius: var(--r-ctl, 8px);
  font-size: 10px; font-weight: 750; text-transform: uppercase; white-space: nowrap;
}
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-stance.buy { color: var(--ink-pv-buy, var(--pv-buy)); }
/* Near: same repair as the lane header above (DARK DELTA item 1) — the link
   ink, not the stance family. */
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-stance.near { color: var(--ink-link, var(--link)); }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-stance.wait { color: var(--ink-pv-wait, var(--pv-wait)); }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-stance.avoid { color: var(--ink-pv-avoid, var(--pv-avoid)); }

.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-expand-wrap {
  display: flex; justify-content: center; padding: 9px 12px 11px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--panel2) 32%, transparent);
}
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-expand {
  height: 35px; padding: 0 14px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--r-ctl, 8px);
  background: var(--panel2); color: var(--text); font-size: 12.5px; font-weight: 650; cursor: pointer;
}
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-expand:hover { border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--text) 30%, var(--line)); transform: translateY(-1px); }

/* ---- Prophet controls / grid / card typography ---------------------------- */

.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-controls { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 7px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-seg { display: inline-flex; gap: 3px; padding: 3px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--r-btn, 10px); background: var(--panel2); }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-seg button {
  height: 36px; padding: 0 14px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: var(--r-ctl, 8px);
  background: transparent; color: var(--muted); font-size: 13.1px; font-weight: 650; cursor: pointer;
}
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-seg button[aria-selected=true] {
  background: var(--panel); border-color: var(--line); color: var(--text);
  box-shadow: 0 1px 4px color-mix(in srgb, var(--bg) 12%, transparent);
}
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-seg button:disabled {
  cursor: default; opacity: .52; box-shadow: none;
}
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-result { color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; white-space: nowrap; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-filter {
  display: none; height: 32px; align-items: center; padding: 0 10px;
  border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--link) 35%, var(--line)); border-radius: var(--r-pill, 999px);
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--link) 7%, transparent); color: var(--text); font-size: 12px; cursor: pointer;
}
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-filter.is-on { display: inline-flex; }

/* ---- Hidden overrides (card.hidden = !show defeats author display rules) --- */

.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-card-grid .pvcard[hidden] { display: none !important; }

/* Server-owned source projection. Before the entitled composer arrives, the
   validated first five owner cards are Top; after adoption, card.hidden is the
   sole grid controller. Table rows retain the same serialized owner identity. */
#ca-v36:not([data-ca-enhanced="true"]) #ca-v36-prophet[data-initial-source="top"] #standouts .cards > .pvcard:nth-of-type(n+6) {
  display: none !important;
}
#ca-v36:not([data-ca-enhanced="true"]) #ca-v36-prophet[data-initial-source="top"] #standouts .cards > .pvcard:nth-of-type(-n+5) {
  border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--link) 20%, var(--line));
}
#ca-v36-prophet[data-active-source="top"] #stocktable-wrap tbody tr[data-prophet-top="false"] {
  display: none !important;
}

.mx-stockdash--ca .prophet-owner-context {
  display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 7px; padding: 10px 0 7px;
  color: var(--muted); font-size: 12.4px; font-weight: 600;
}
.mx-stockdash--ca .prophet-owner-context [data-prophet-help] { display: inline-flex; flex: none; }

.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-card-grid {
  display: block; padding: 14px;
}
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-card-grid .pvcard {
  min-width: 0; height: 100%; font-family: var(--font-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, Inter, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif);
  transition: transform .15s ease, box-shadow .15s ease, border-color .15s ease;
}
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-card-grid .pvcard:hover { transform: translateY(-2px); }

/* The owner board remains in place, so its show-more state stays authoritative. */

.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-card-grid .pv-chart svg { height: 82px !important; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-card-grid .pv-bd { padding: 14px 14px 12px !important; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-card-grid .pv-tk { font-family: var(--font-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, Inter, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif) !important; font-size: 16.7px !important; font-weight: 700 !important; letter-spacing: -.012em !important; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-card-grid .pv-nm { font-family: var(--font-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, Inter, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif) !important; font-size: 12.5px !important; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-card-grid .pv-ind { font-size: 11.1px !important; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-card-grid .pv-edge { font-family: var(--font-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, Inter, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif) !important; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-card-grid .pv-edn { font-size: 16px !important; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-card-grid .nb-px.pv-px { font-family: var(--font-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, Inter, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif) !important; font-size: 15.8px !important; font-weight: 750 !important; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-card-grid .nb-chg.pv-chg { font-family: var(--font-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, Inter, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif) !important; font-size: 13.4px !important; font-weight: 750 !important; }

/* Canada quote colors: Western green-up/red-down, unchanged even under ZH. */
.mx-stockdash--ca .nb-chg.up,
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-table .nb-chg.up { color: var(--ok) !important; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .nb-chg.down,
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-table .nb-chg.down { color: var(--act) !important; }

.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-card-grid .pv-chip { font-size: 10.8px !important; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-card-grid .pv-life-w,
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-card-grid .pv-stl { font-size: 11.1px !important; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-card-grid .pv-zn { min-height: 42px !important; font-size: 11.6px !important; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-card-grid .pv-znr,
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-card-grid .pv-znm { font-family: var(--font-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, Inter, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif) !important; font-size: 11.8px !important; }

.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-card-grid .ca-v36-top-pick {
  border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--link) 20%, var(--line));
  box-shadow:
    0 0 0 1px color-mix(in srgb, var(--link) 8%, transparent),
    0 0 24px -16px color-mix(in srgb, var(--link) 42%, transparent),
    0 8px 24px -20px color-mix(in srgb, var(--bg) 55%, transparent);
}

.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-empty { grid-column: 1 / -1; padding: 36px 16px; text-align: center; color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-empty-switch {
  display: block; margin: 10px auto 0; height: 31px; padding: 0 13px;
  border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--r-ctl, 8px);
  background: var(--panel2); color: var(--text); font-size: 11.8px; font-weight: 650; cursor: pointer;
}
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-empty-switch:hover { border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--text) 30%, var(--line)); transform: translateY(-1px); }

/* ---- Table / live quote presentation --------------------------------------- */

.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-table { padding: 12px 14px 15px; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-table[hidden] { display: none !important; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-table #stocktable-wrap { display: block !important; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-table .stf-row,
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-table .stf-controls { font-family: var(--font-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, Inter, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif) !important; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-table :is(input, select, button) { min-height: 38px; font-size: 12.8px !important; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-table .st-table { font-family: var(--font-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, Inter, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif) !important; font-size: 13.3px !important; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-table .st-table th { font-size: 11px !important; padding: 11px 10px !important; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-table .st-table td { padding: 11px 10px !important; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-table .st-table td:nth-child(2) b { font-family: var(--font-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, Inter, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif) !important; font-size: 13.8px; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-table-live { display: inline-flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 8px; white-space: nowrap; font-family: var(--font-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, Inter, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif); }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-table-live .nb-px { font-size: 14.8px; font-weight: 700; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-table-live .nb-chg { font-size: 12.7px; font-weight: 750; }
.mx-stockdash--ca #stocktable-wrap tr.ca-v36-hidden { display: none !important; }

/* ---- Research Tools --------------------------------------------------------- */

.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-tools { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; padding: 11px 14px; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-tools b { font-size: 12.8px; margin-right: 2px; }
.mx-stockdash--ca .ca-v36-tool {
  height: 37px; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; padding: 0 12px;
  border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--r-ctl, 8px);
