rules.new:
/* ── font stacks ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   --font-ui   : primary UI stack. San Francisco leads via the system keywords
                 — SF cannot be self-hosted (Apple's licence bars webfont
                 redistribution), and naming no optical variant lets SF pick
                 Text/Display itself. Inter follows as the carrier elsewhere,
                 AHEAD of Segoe UI / Roboto so non-Apple gets the house face.
   --font-mono : figures, tickers, code, axis ticks. ui-monospace resolves to
                 SF Mono (macOS/iOS), Consolas (Windows) — no download. */
--font-ui: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, Inter, "Segoe UI", Roboto,
  "Helvetica Neue", "PingFang SC", "Hiragino Sans GB", "Microsoft YaHei",
  "Noto Sans CJK SC", sans-serif;
--font-mono: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", SFMono-Regular, "Cascadia Mono",
  Menlo, Consolas, "DejaVu Sans Mono", monospace;
/* --num : numeric-face alias. Referenced ~30× on the macro dashboard for its
   data numerals; body.page-macro overrides it to a mono terminal face on its
   own scope. This :root default keeps the token valid everywhere else (a bare
   `font-family:var(--num)` is otherwise an invalid decl on non-macro pages). */
--num: var(--font-ui);
/* ── type ramp — the SITE type scale (design-system packet PR-0(a)) ─────────
   11 deliberate steps, promoted VERBATIM out of body.page-macro
   (dashboard.html.j2) where it was born; body.estate (seo_base) carried a
   byte-identical copy and leader_radar/intraday_flow carried near-copies.
   Promotion only — no value was retuned; the pages that differ keep a
   documented local override rather than being silently re-sized.

   It must live at :root, NOT on a body class. body.page-stocks (the Prophet
   board) never declared the ramp and inherits it ONLY through :root — a
   body-class home would leave every Prophet surface off the scale. Same for
   the calculators and the seo_* estate children, which use var(--fs-*)
   without declaring it and today resolve it through their base template. */
--fs-display:46px;   /* hero verdict word          */
--fs-num-xl:38px;    /* the big board scores        */
--fs-h1:28px;        /* page / hero title           */
--fs-num-lg:22px;    /* secondary big numerals      */
--fs-h2:17px;        /* panel section titles        */
--fs-md:15px;        /* lead body / strong figures  */
--fs-body:14px;      /* base copy                   */
--fs-h3:14px;        /* subsection titles           */
--fs-sm:12.5px;      /* secondary copy / table body */
--fs-label:11px;     /* MONO eyebrows · caps        */
--fs-micro:10px;     /* dense ticks · table heads   */
--bg: #0f1115; --panel: #181b21; --panel2: #1e222a; --text: #d7dce3;
--muted: #8b93a1;
/* Estate contrast pass 2026-08-03: #2a2f3a measured 1.13–1.29:1 against the
   dark panels — fainter than the LIGHT theme's raised 1.6 floor, inverted from
   how the two themes should sit. #3a4150 lands containers at 1.56–1.85 across
   the estate's dark surfaces, the same perceptual band as light. */
--line: #3a4150;
--line-quiet: #272C35;
--q1: #2e9e4f; --q2: #d4a017; --q3: #d04545; --q4: #3f78d8;
--warn: #e0a030; --act: #e05555; --ok: #3da564;
/* Freshness/recency snapshot of --ok, computed HERE (unremapped). It inherits
   RESOLVED, so a .fresh chip inside html[data-lang="zh"] .rrx / .igs keeps the
   status green when those scopes remap --ok onto --up. Do not redeclare this
   alias inside .rrx/.igs — that would re-resolve against the remapped --ok. */
--fresh-ok: var(--ok);
--up: #45b873; --down: #e06464; --orange: #e08b45;
--info: #5b9bf0; --link: #7aa7e0;
--g-cold: #4d8df0; --g-hot: #e0a23c; --g-mid: #3a4150;
/* ── prophet-card verb hues (_prophet_card.html.j2) ─────────────────────────
   One hue per card state: buy/near/wait/hold/avoid. English uses the Western
   green-up/red-down convention. Chinese mode rebinds only these Prophet tokens
   onto the site's Asia-aware --up/--down pair below, so every Prophet board
   becomes red-bullish/green-bearish without recolouring non-Prophet status UI.

   STANCE IS NOT DIRECTION (DA-002 cure, C8-C — reference board.css:48/:83/:110).
   --pv-buy used to be the literal #45b873, byte-identical to --up above: a Buy
   chip and a +2.1% change printed the SAME ink, so one colour on one card meant
   two different things and no reader could tell the call from the tape. Stance
   now sits a deliberate tone off the direction ink it belongs to — same semantic
   family, visibly not the same colour. Derived FROM --up rather than hand-picked
   so the zh flip stays structural: 红涨绿跌 needs no second table below, and a
   future --up nudge carries the stance with it instead of silently re-colliding.
   Deepening toward --text also RAISES contrast for BUY on both planes, on all four
   of its consumers, in all four quadrants. It does not do so uniformly: Near, which
   is now mixed toward --muted rather than carrying its own hue, regresses on the
   two DARK quadrants — 8 pairs, worst -0.94 (en/dark .pv-znl 8.12 -> 7.18) — and
   every one of them still clears AA by a margin. Do not restate this as a blanket
   improvement; the measured plane is what governs (measured by
   tests/test_prophet_verb_ink_contrast.py, all 5 verbs x 4 consumers x 4
   theme/lang quadrants; re-measure with mockups/refs/prophet_verb_ink/probe_pv_ink.py).
   Separation, CIELAB dE, raw token / text ink, all eight readings 0.00 before:
     en-light 30.5 / 5.6 · zh-light 35.1 / 23.3 · en-dark 10.1 / 10.1 · zh-dark 12.5 / 12.5
   en/light's 5.6 is the thinnest and is INHERITED, not chosen: light's --ink-mix-up
   is 62% and this mix is 54% — two points on one axis, so those two inks are close
   by construction. It clears the ~2.3 just-noticeable threshold and the two never
   take the same form (Buy is a solid pill, the change is small text), but it is the
   quadrant to re-open first if the separation is ever judged too thin.

   --pv-near follows --pv-buy rather than carrying its own literal, and that is
   forced, not tidy: at the old literal #63c08d, Near landed within ~4/255 per
   channel of the retuned Buy, i.e. curing DA-002 alone would have replaced a
   stance/direction collision with a Buy/Near one. Mixing toward --muted keeps
   Near reading as the softer call at every point on the ramp. */
--pv-buy: color-mix(in srgb, var(--up) 82%, var(--text));
--pv-near: color-mix(in srgb, var(--pv-buy) 70%, var(--muted));
--pv-wait: #e0a030;
--pv-hold: #8b93a1; --pv-avoid: #e06464;
/* Prophet setup-detail modal tokens: literal color decisions live in the palette, not component CSS. */
--pv-dialog-shadow: 0 18px 60px rgba(0,0,0,.2666667);
--pv-dialog-backdrop: rgba(0,0,0,.5333333);
--chart-bg: transparent;
--card-shadow: 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,.02);
--popover-shadow: 0 6px 18px rgba(0,0,0,.5);
/* ── custom scrollbars ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Thumb tint derived from --muted so it adapts to dark / light / zh with no
   per-theme override (--info gives the drag-state a branded accent). Consumed
   by the global scrollbar rules further down and mirrored (with fallbacks) by
   theme.js for the self-contained pages that don't link this file. */
--sb-thumb: color-mix(in srgb, var(--muted) 34%, transparent);
--sb-thumb-hover: color-mix(in srgb, var(--muted) 60%, transparent);
--sb-thumb-active: color-mix(in srgb, var(--info) 62%, var(--muted));
/* ── frosted-glass popover system ───────────────────────────────────────────
   ONE token set shared by every floating menu surface — the top-nav dropdowns,
   the Research mega-menu, the global-search suggestions, the gear settings
   popover, the bell alert popover and the fired-alerts popup — so they all read
   as a single design family. backdrop-filter blurs the aurora + page behind the
   panel; the translucent fill lets that colour bleed through. Opacity + shadow
   are re-tuned per theme in the light block below. The self-contained vector
   family (no theme.css) mirrors these values inline in _vector_polish.html.j2
   and theme.js, so keep the three in sync if you retune the glass. */
--glass-bg: color-mix(in srgb, var(--panel) 86%, transparent);
--glass-brd: color-mix(in srgb, var(--text) 14%, transparent);
--glass-blur: saturate(180%) blur(22px);
--glass-shadow: 0 24px 64px -22px rgba(3,7,18,.74), 0 10px 26px -12px rgba(3,7,18,.55),
  inset 0 1px 0 color-mix(in srgb,#fff 10%,transparent);
/* ── gbtn: house glass-button token set (macro sweep 2026-07) ──────────────
   The default button surface for the whole site — a frosted pill that reads as
   one family with the glass popovers above. Fill/border derive from --panel2 /
   --text via color-mix so dark, light and the zh swap all resolve at paint. */
--gbtn-bg:        color-mix(in srgb, var(--panel2) 52%, transparent);
--gbtn-bg-hover:  color-mix(in srgb, var(--panel2) 76%, transparent);
--gbtn-brd:       color-mix(in srgb, var(--text) 12%, transparent);
--gbtn-brd-hover: color-mix(in srgb, var(--text) 24%, transparent);
--gbtn-sheen:     rgba(255,255,255,.09);
/* Retained evidence states share the canonical theme surfaces. */
--surface-warn-subtle: color-mix(in srgb, var(--warn) 6%, var(--panel));
/* Quiet semantic surfaces; labels retain the status and directional meaning. */
--surface-info-subtle: color-mix(in srgb, var(--info) 6%, var(--panel));
--surface-ok-subtle: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ok) 6%, var(--panel));
--surface-act-subtle: color-mix(in srgb, var(--act) 6%, var(--panel));
--surface-up-subtle: color-mix(in srgb, var(--up) 8%, var(--panel));
--surface-down-subtle: color-mix(in srgb, var(--down) 8%, var(--panel));
--text-on-dark: #fff;
--text-on-light: #1a1a1a;
