/* ── THE SIX-WEIGHT LIFECYCLE GRAMMAR ────────────────────────────────────────
   ONE grammar, two scales, in two different places:
     .mx-cap  — a full-bleed 3px cap at the top of a LADDER CELL. Ladder only:
                the card's top cap was repealed so it would stop competing with
                the chart for the card's head, and that repeal is law. The cap's
                base rule and its content:"" are therefore SCOPED to .mx-cell,
                which makes the law structural — a .mx-cap emitted anywhere else
                generates no box at all rather than a stray 3px artefact.
     .mx-mark — the same six weights at inline scale (26x8px), for the card's
                lifecycle fact column, the table cell and the absence line.
   So the ladder-to-card link is carried by the INLINE MARK, not by a shared cap:
   the same six weights on both surfaces, each at the scale that surface can
   afford. Identical grammar, deliberately non-identical geometry. */
.mx-cell > .mx-cap { position:absolute; top:0; left:0; right:0; height:3px;
